<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="skill">carpentry</ansi> (skill)

Carpentry is woodworking: turning planks and timber into weapons, shields,
bows and arrows, furniture and fittings. It is governed by
<ansi fg="yellow">Dexterity</ansi>, since joinery and shaping reward a steady, precise hand.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Requirements ━━━</ansi>

  Station:   A <ansi fg="yellow">woodworking bench</ansi> must be in the room with you.
             Look for one at the Woodworker's House in Amber Valley, the
             Timber Yard at Kilnreach, the Lumber Camp on Cascade Pass Road,
             the Woodcutter's Camp on the North Road, and the Fletcher's Ledge
             in Pothole Coulee.
  Materials: Wooden planks, with leather strips for grips and bindings.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Known Recipes ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">wooden-club</ansi>   A simple hardwood club (minimum 0).

More carpentry is on the way: sawing logs into planks and staves, bows,
arrows, wooden shields and furniture.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Skill Progression ━━━</ansi>

Carpentry improves through use. Each completed craft attempt (success or
failure) has a chance to advance the skill.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Commands ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">craft list</ansi>          Show all recipes, including carpentry ones, with status.
  <ansi fg="command">craft <recipe></ansi>      Begin crafting a carpentry recipe.
  <ansi fg="command">skills</ansi>              Check your current carpentry skill level.

<ansi fg="yellow">See Also:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">help craft</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help skills</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help tools</ansi>
